  "review": {
    "review": "The hero was alive at 33/70 HP when planning stopped, not killed. Decisions 3180–3181 selected and executed a known, uncursed prismatic-light staff zap at the observed DM-100. The accepted transition at log line 8976 consumed one charge; the next observation gained six experience in one turn, removed the caster and showed a scroll at its square. Arcane Vision was already learned. The initiating bookkeeping defect discarded attack capture because this newly seen enemy had no health bar, and the existing tracked-bolt kill receipt did not support prismatic light. Consequently the remembered lightning lane survived the kill and the early safety selector blocked all later progress arbitration at decision 3182 (log lines 8977–8978). This is stronger evidence than disappearance alone: pinned game source confirms single-target damage and tracking before damage. An isolated reconstruction of only the targeting/receipt bookkeeping matches both recorded inputs; it is not a reconstruction of the entire run. The proposed focused correction retains receipt-only capture without inventing health, and recognizes this strictly verified tracked prismatic kill. The new regression fails twice on original code and passes on the candidate; all 2,267 discovered tests pass, with four skipped. This establishes retirement of the matching phantom threat, not subsequent loot collection, safe movement or survival. Earlier blinded-caster receipts and loot-routing oscillation remain outside this correction. The played source diff is empty, so no recorded improvements are attributed.",
    "learnings": "A missing enemy health bar must not erase independently verifiable kill evidence. For a known uncursed prismatic zap, require consumed charge, one-turn six-XP receipt, Arcane Vision, a freshly observed clear ray, a single eligible target and no surviving caster before retiring its matching lightning memory. Keep ambiguous sightings, mandatory pickups, hazard gates and terminal planner exhaustion unchanged."
  },
